[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943776375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107140#issuecomment-2943776375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107140","id":2943776375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vdnZ3","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T11:14:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T11:14:29Z","body":"This seems unlikely to be an issue with Godot 3.x (but not impossible), essentially we just render to opengl and swap buffers afaik.\n\nA quick google search reveals loads of results for flickering with dual monitors with Nvidia.\nhttps://www.google.com/search?q=nvidia+flickering+dual+monitors\n\nAs well as Godot, it can be e.g: \n* a driver issue\n* a GPU hardware issue\n* monitor issue\n* OS issue\n\nIt sounds like playing with your nvidia settings may well give some joy.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943776375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hoo